# Frozen byte-identity baseline for APPLIED migrations.
#
# Every migration in this list has been run against a real database. Supabase
# records their checksums, so editing one does not "fix" anything — it
# desynchronises the repository from every environment that has already
# migrated. There is no supported way to change an applied migration; the only
# forward move is a new one.
#
# scripts/verify-db-service-role.sh and scripts/verify-learn-progress-db.sh both
# fail if any line here stops matching, as do the ROAS and API-CORS gates. This
# is an artifact property, not a branch diff, so it keeps holding after a branch
# merges and as later migrations are added.
#
# A migration joins this list in the work package that follows its deployment,
# never in the one that authors it — an unapplied migration is still editable in
# review, and freezing it early would be a lie about what the database has seen.
#
# DB-SERVICE-ROLE-1 froze the first 37. LEARN-PROGRESS-DB-1 added
# 20260828000100 once the Founder had applied it to publish the ROAS curriculum.
# 20260829000100 is deliberately ABSENT: it is this package's repair and has not
# been deployed.
#
# Paths are relative to the repository root, which is where the gates run.
